ArtificialCanineEngine (ACE) uses data derived from the following sources.
Raw data is not included in this repository.

Darwin's Ark
  Morrill K. et al. (2022). Ancestry-inclusive dog genomics challenges
  popular breed stereotypes. Science 376, eabk0639.
  Data: Zenodo 6522639; Dryad doi:10.5061/dryad.g4f4qrfr0
  License: CC0 1.0
  Used in: data/derived/personality_prior.json,
           data/derived/emotion_prior.json

VIDOPET (Vienna Dog Personality Test) database
  Turcsán B., Wallis L., Virányi Z., Range F., Müller C. A., Huber L.,
  Riemer S. (2018). Personality traits in companion dogs: Results from the
  VIDOPET. PLOS ONE 13(4): e0195448. doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0195448
  Data: Figshare doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.5477932.v2
  License: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
  Used in: data/derived/vidopet_targets.json
  Changes: data/derived/vidopet_targets.json holds summary statistics
  computed from the database (rank correlations with bootstrap intervals,
  coefficients of variation, questionnaire reliabilities), not the
  original records.

C-BARQ survey data on dog behavior and temperament
  Ghirlanda S., Acerbi A., Herzog H., Serpell J. A. (2013). C-BARQ survey
  on dog behavior and temperament. Questionnaire described in Duffy D. L. &
  Serpell J. A. (2012), Applied Animal Behaviour Science 138: 99-109.
  Data: Figshare doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.715896.v1
  License: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
  Used in: data/derived/emotion_prior.json
  Changes: data/derived/emotion_prior.json uses summary statistics computed
  from the dataset (golden retriever vs all-dog differences in standard
  deviation units), not the original records.
